  "summary": "A borehole (well) pump in which both the multistage pump and its electric motor are lowered into the well below the water level and hang from the riser pipe. The sealed, water-filled motor sits at the bottom so water flowing past to the intake cools it; the pump stages above lift water up the riser. A built-in check valve keeps the riser full when the pump stops. No long line shaft is needed, so very deep wells can be served.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Rotodynamic, mixed/radial flow diffuser stages",
    "configuration": "Submersible, multistage, close-coupled motor below pump"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "well_size": "150 mm (6 in) borehole",
    "stages": 6,
    "motor": "Water-filled rewindable 6 in motor with tilting-pad thrust bearing and pressure-equalising diaphragm (NEMA/ISO interface flange)",
    "cooling_note": "Minimum flow velocity past the motor (often ~0.08–0.15 m/s per manufacturer) is required; fit a flow sleeve if water enters from above."
  },
